          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "GM lays off hundreds of IT workers and rehires for AI-native roles in major workforce pivot",
            "articleSection": "Job Evolution",
            "abstract": "General Motors has laid off hundreds of IT employees and is actively replacing them with workers skilled in AI-native development, data engineering, cloud-based engineering, agent and model development, and prompt engineering. The move signals that one of America's largest manufacturers is treating AI competency as a core job requirement rather than a specialist add-on. This is one of the most concrete examples yet of a major non-tech corporation restructuring its entire IT workforce around AI skills.",
            "url": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/11/gm-just-laid-off-hundreds-of-it-workers-to-hire-those-with-stronger-ai-skills/",
            "publisher": {
